§§ `פרק ב' §1 — עובד, עובד קבוע, עובד קיים, עובד חדש`

-- akn:chp_2 The heading of chapter ב'.
-- akn:chp_2__art_1 The heading of §1: employee, permanent, existing and new employee.
-- akn:chp_2__art_1__para_a The heading "in the State's service".
-- akn:chp_2__art_1__para_b The heading "in the Centre of Local Government".
-- akn:chp_2__art_1__para_c The heading "in the three large cities".
-- akn:chp_2__art_1__para_c/p2 The heading "Tel Aviv municipality".
-- akn:chp_2__art_1__para_c/p7 The heading "Jerusalem municipality".
-- akn:chp_2__art_1__para_c__hc_2/p2 The heading "Haifa municipality".
-- akn:chp_2__art_1__para_d The heading "in the Hebrew University".
-- akn:chp_2__art_1__para_d/p6 The heading "in the Technion".
-- akn:chp_2__art_1__para_e The heading "in the Centre of Regional Councils, in the fire-service associations".
-- akn:chp_2__art_1__para_f The heading "the Union of Religious Councils".
-- akn:chp_2__art_1__para_g The heading "in the Employment Service".
-- akn:chp_2__art_1__para_h The heading "the National Insurance Institute".

@desc The employers of the agreement of 3.3.1999, as its definitions tell them apart.
DECLARE `1999 transition employer` IS ONE OF
    `the State's service`
    `a local authority of the Centre`
    `a regional council`
    `a fire-service association of towns`
    `the Tel Aviv municipality`
    `the Jerusalem municipality`
    `the Haifa municipality`
    `the Hebrew University`
    `the Technion`
    `a religious council`
    `the Employment Service`
    `the National Insurance Institute`

@desc What the definitions of chapter ב' §1 ask of an employee, at the determining date.
DECLARE `1999 employee facts` HAS
    `left out of "עובד" at his employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc one of the exceptions his employer's definition of "עובד" lists: a special contract (תקנה 1(3) or 1(18)), service the Appointments Law does not reach (§2(3)–(6), §4), the seniors' agreement, a personal contract with managers' insurance, hourly or daily work, and so on
    `employed at the determining date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `insured in an accrual pension at the determining date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `appointed or tenured by the determining date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc a letter of appointment (§17 of the Appointments Law; the Employment Service's or the Institute's), a letter of tenure, a permanent appointment or tenure, as his employer's definition says
    `employed under a written permit of §§37, 38 or 39א` IS A BOOLEAN @desc in the State's service
    `on probation in a standard post` IS A BOOLEAN @desc the Employment Service, the Institute (a temporary-employment approval), the Hebrew University
    `appointed or tenured after the determining date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a manual worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Tel Aviv: "עובד כפיים"; any other is "עובד מקצועי"
    `months employed by the employer` IS A NUMBER @desc at the determining date
    `in a standard post` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Jerusalem, Haifa: "משרה תקנית"
    `months in that post` IS A NUMBER @desc at the determining date
    `in a transient post` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Tel Aviv: "משרת חולפת"
    `completed a year with the authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc local authorities
    `chose an accrual pension on tenure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc the Technion
    `completed his probation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc religious councils: 6 months, or 9 where extended
    `on a fixed-term personal contract` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Haifa

DECLARE `1999 employee status` IS ONE OF
    `a permanent employee`
    `an existing employee`
    `a new employee`
    `not an employee of the 1999 agreement`

-- (א) the State's service: "עובד", one whose pay is by a scale, save one on
-- a special contract under regulation 1(3) or 1(18), one the Appointments
-- Law does not reach by its §2(3)–(5), one in an enterprise outside it by
-- §2(6) insured in an accrual pension by its own collective agreement, and
-- one in an enterprise or unit the government exempted under §4 until the
-- signing. "עובד קבוע": employed at the determining date and appointed by a
-- letter under §17 before it — and, for this agreement only, one employed
-- at it under a written permit of §37, §38 or §39א. "עובד קיים": employed at
-- it, his pension rights insured at it in an accrual pension. "עובד חדש":
-- one taken on after it, entitled to an accrual pension.
-- F-pension-1999-b: the definitions overlap — one employed under a permit
-- whose rights are insured in an accrual pension is both permanent and
-- existing. The reading adopted (convention precedence.specific): the
-- express "for this agreement only" makes him permanent, as the bill of
-- annex ה' (§107ב(ד)) keeps him under the Pensions Law.
@ref akn:chp_2__art_1__para_a/p2 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_a__subpara_1 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_a__subpara_2 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_a__subpara_3 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_a__subpara_4 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_a__hc_1/p1 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_a__hc_2/p1 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_a__hc_3/p1
GIVEN f IS A `1999 employee facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `permanent in the State's service by the 1999 definition` f IF
        f's `employed at the determining date`
    AND (f's `appointed or tenured by the determining date` OR f's `employed under a written permit of §§37, 38 or 39א`)

-- (ב) the local authorities: "עובד", save one on the seniors' agreement
-- (the joint circular of 23.3.93) or a special contract; "עובד קבוע":
-- employed at the determining date, save an existing one; "עובד קיים":
-- employed at it and insured in an accrual pension, and one who had not
-- completed a year at it and was not so insured; "עובד חדש": taken on after
-- it. (ה): the regional councils and the fire-service associations, the
-- same.
@ref akn:chp_2__art_1__para_b/p2 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_b/p3 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_b/p4 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_b/p5 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_e/p2
GIVEN f IS A `1999 employee facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `existing at a local authority by the 1999 definition` f IF
        f's `employed at the determining date`
    AND (   f's `insured in an accrual pension at the determining date`
         OR NOT f's `completed a year with the authority`)

-- (ג) Tel Aviv: "עובד קבוע": employed on the eve with a letter of tenure on
-- the eve, or a manual worker employed more than 24 months, or a
-- professional one more than 18; "עובד קיים": taken on by the eve without a
-- letter of tenure, save those manual and professional workers — "and
-- including" one in a transient post. F-pension-1999-c: a transient post
-- held more than 24 (or 18) months is in both. The reading adopted
-- (convention precedence.specific): the express "ולרבות" makes him existing.
@ref akn:chp_2__art_1__para_c/p3 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_c/p4 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_c/p5 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_c/p6
GIVEN f IS A `1999 employee facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `permanent in Tel Aviv by the 1999 definition, as printed` f IF
        f's `employed at the determining date`
    AND (   f's `appointed or tenured by the determining date`
         OR (f's `a manual worker` AND f's `months employed by the employer` `is above` 24)
         OR ((NOT f's `a manual worker`) AND f's `months employed by the employer` `is above` 18))

GIVEN f IS A `1999 employee facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `existing in Tel Aviv by the 1999 definition, as printed` f IF
        f's `employed at the determining date`
    AND (   f's `in a transient post`
         OR NOT `permanent in Tel Aviv by the 1999 definition, as printed` f)

-- Jerusalem: "עובד", save one on a personal contract insured in managers'
-- insurance or an accrual pension, and one on a special contract with no
-- pension; "עובד קבוע": employed at the determining date and (1) in a
-- standard post with a permanent appointment by it, (2) in a standard post
-- more than a year and appointed after it, or (3) in a non-standard post
-- and employed more than 4 years; "עובד קיים": in a standard post up to a
-- year and not yet appointed, or in a non-standard post up to 4 years.
@ref akn:chp_2__art_1__para_c/p8 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_c/p9 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_c__subpara_1 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_c__subpara_2 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_c__subpara_3 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_c__hc_1/p1 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_c__hc_2/p1
GIVEN f IS A `1999 employee facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `permanent in Jerusalem by the 1999 definition` f IF
        f's `employed at the determining date`
    AND (   (f's `in a standard post` AND f's `appointed or tenured by the determining date`)
         OR (f's `in a standard post` AND f's `months in that post` `is above` 12 AND f's `appointed or tenured after the determining date`)
         OR ((NOT f's `in a standard post`) AND f's `months employed by the employer` `is above` 48))

-- Haifa: "עובד", save one on the seniors' agreement; "עובד קבוע": in a
-- standard post at the determining date with a letter of tenure by it, or
-- in a standard post more than 24 months; "עובד קיים": in a standard post
-- without such a letter, save the one of more than 24 months, and one on a
-- fixed-term personal contract.
@ref akn:chp_2__art_1__para_c__hc_3/p1 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_c__hc_4/p1 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_c__hc_4/p2 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_c__hc_5/p1
GIVEN f IS A `1999 employee facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `permanent in Haifa by the 1999 definition` f IF
        f's `employed at the determining date`
    AND f's `in a standard post`
    AND (f's `appointed or tenured by the determining date` OR f's `months in that post` `is above` 24)

-- (ד) the Hebrew University: "עובד", save hourly and daily workers (no
-- pension insurance) and seniors on a special contract; "עובד קבוע":
-- appointed permanent by the determining date — or employed at it 10 years
-- or more, or on probation in a standard post, and appointed after it, from
-- the appointment only; "עובד קיים": insured in an accrual pension at it,
-- those two among them until they are appointed. The Technion: "עובד", save
-- hourly workers and personal contracts; "עובד קבוע": tenured, or on
-- probation for tenure, by the special agreement of 30.5.79, save one who
-- chose an accrual pension on tenure; "עובד קיים": a temporary employee in
-- an accrual pension, or the one who so chose.
@ref akn:chp_2__art_1__para_d/p2 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_d/p3 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_d/p4 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_d/p5 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_d/p7 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_d/p8 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_d/p9 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_d/p10
GIVEN f IS A `1999 employee facts`, `appointed yet` IS A BOOLEAN @desc on the day asked about
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `permanent at the Hebrew University by the 1999 definition` f `appointed yet` IF
        f's `employed at the determining date`
    AND (   f's `appointed or tenured by the determining date`
         OR (    (f's `months employed by the employer` AT LEAST 120 OR f's `on probation in a standard post`)
             AND f's `appointed or tenured after the determining date`
             AND `appointed yet`))

GIVEN f IS A `1999 employee facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `permanent at the Technion by the 1999 definition` f IF
        f's `employed at the determining date`
    AND f's `appointed or tenured by the determining date`
    AND NOT f's `chose an accrual pension on tenure`

-- (ו) the religious councils: "עובד קבוע": one who completed by the
-- determining date the probation of 6 months, or 9 where extended, of the
-- local authorities' work constitution; "עובד קיים": any other employed at
-- it. (ז) the Employment Service and (ח) the Institute: "עובד", save one on
-- a special contract (§17 of the Employment Service Law; §22(ב) of the
-- National Insurance Law); "עובד קבוע": appointed by a letter of the
-- Service, or of the Institute, by the determining date, or in a standard
-- post on probation by a temporary-employment approval; "עובד קיים": in the
-- Service, insured in an accrual pension; in the Institute, one with a
-- contract of employment by it, save a permanent one.
@ref akn:chp_2__art_1__para_f/p2 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_f/p3 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_f/p4 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_f/p5 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_g/p2 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_g/p3 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_g/p4 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_g/p5 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_g/p6 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_h/p2 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_h/p3 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_h/p4 akn:chp_2__art_1__para_h/p5
GIVEN f IS A `1999 employee facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `permanent in the Service or the Institute by the 1999 definition` f IF
        f's `employed at the determining date`
    AND (f's `appointed or tenured by the determining date` OR f's `on probation in a standard post`)

-- The status, employer by employer. A new employee is one taken on after
-- the determining date, at every employer; one left out of "עובד" is none.
GIVEN e IS A `1999 transition employer`, f IS A `1999 employee facts`, `appointed yet` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `1999 employee status`
DECIDE `the 1999 status of` e f `appointed yet` IS
    BRANCH
        IF f's `left out of "עובד" at his employer` THEN `not an employee of the 1999 agreement`
        IF NOT f's `employed at the determining date` THEN `a new employee`
        IF permanent THEN `a permanent employee`
        IF existing THEN `an existing employee`
        OTHERWISE `not an employee of the 1999 agreement`
    WHERE
        local MEANS
                e EQUALS `a local authority of the Centre`
             OR e EQUALS `a regional council`
             OR e EQUALS `a fire-service association of towns`
        permanent MEANS
            CONSIDER e
            WHEN `the State's service` THEN `permanent in the State's service by the 1999 definition` f
            WHEN `the Tel Aviv municipality` THEN `permanent in Tel Aviv by the 1999 definition, as printed` f AND NOT f's `in a transient post`
            WHEN `the Jerusalem municipality` THEN `permanent in Jerusalem by the 1999 definition` f
            WHEN `the Haifa municipality` THEN `permanent in Haifa by the 1999 definition` f AND NOT f's `on a fixed-term personal contract`
            WHEN `the Hebrew University` THEN `permanent at the Hebrew University by the 1999 definition` f `appointed yet`
            WHEN `the Technion` THEN `permanent at the Technion by the 1999 definition` f
            WHEN `a religious council` THEN f's `completed his probation`
            WHEN `the Employment Service` THEN `permanent in the Service or the Institute by the 1999 definition` f
            WHEN `the National Insurance Institute` THEN `permanent in the Service or the Institute by the 1999 definition` f
            OTHERWISE local AND NOT `existing at a local authority by the 1999 definition` f
        existing MEANS
            CONSIDER e
            WHEN `the State's service` THEN f's `insured in an accrual pension at the determining date`
            WHEN `the Tel Aviv municipality` THEN `existing in Tel Aviv by the 1999 definition, as printed` f
            WHEN `the Hebrew University` THEN f's `insured in an accrual pension at the determining date`
            WHEN `the Technion` THEN f's `insured in an accrual pension at the determining date` OR f's `chose an accrual pension on tenure`
            WHEN `the Employment Service` THEN f's `insured in an accrual pension at the determining date`
            OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `פרק ב' §2 — המועד הקובע`

-- akn:chp_2__art_2 The heading of §2, the determining date.
-- akn:chp_2__art_2__para_a The heading "in the State's service, the Employment Service and the National Insurance Institute".
-- akn:chp_2__art_2__para_b The heading of (ב): the local authorities, the three large cities, the regional councils, the religious councils and the fire-service associations.
-- akn:chp_2__art_2__para_c The heading "in the Hebrew University and the Technion".

-- (א)(1): in the State, the Service and the Institute, the date set under
-- the Pensions Law, as amended for this agreement — the Finance Minister to
-- publish one no later than the end of two months after the month the
-- amendment comes into force, and not back in time; (2) in a workplace of
-- annex א', the date set under that law, at the move of the workplace's
-- employees another union represents.
@ref akn:chp_2__art_2__para_a__subpara_1 akn:chp_2__art_2__para_a__subpara_1/p2 akn:chp_2__art_2__para_a__subpara_2
GIVEN `the month the amendment comes into force` IS A DATE @desc any day of that month
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the latest determining date the Finance Minister may publish` `the month the amendment comes into force` IS
    `the first of the month after` 2 `months after the month of` `the month the amendment comes into force`

`publishing the State's determining date` MEANS
    PARTY `the Treasury`
    MUST  `publish the determining date under the Pensions Law`

-- (ב)(1): at the local authorities and the others of (ב), the first of the
-- month after the end of 3 months from the month the agreement was signed;
-- (2) in a workplace of annex ב', the move of the other union's employees.
-- "תום 3 חודשיים מהחודש שבו נחתם": the three months after the month of
-- signing (convention dates.months-from-month).
@ref akn:chp_2__art_2__para_b__subpara_1 akn:chp_2__art_2__para_b__subpara_2
`the local authorities' determining date` MEANS
    `the first of the month after` 3 `months after the month of` `the pension-transition agreement was signed on`

-- (ג): at the two universities, the move of the senior academic staff.
-- ¶3: for the employees of (א)(2), (ב)(2) and (ג) the union may notify the
-- employer at any time of its wish for an earlier date; then (1) for (ב)(2)
-- and (ג), the first of the month after the end of two months from the
-- month of the notice; (2) for (א)(2), the date under the Pensions Law,
-- published no later than the end of two months from that month, and not
-- before the law comes into force.
@ref akn:chp_2__art_2__para_c/p2 akn:chp_2__art_2__para_c/p3 akn:chp_2__art_2__para_c__subpara_1 akn:chp_2__art_2__para_c__subpara_2
GIVEN `the union's notice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the earlier determining date the union's notice sets` `the union's notice` IS
    `the first of the month after` 2 `months after the month of` `the union's notice`

-- The first of the month after the end of n months from the month of a
-- day: the months counted are those after it (convention
-- dates.months-from-month).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the first of the month after` n `months after the month of` d IS
    DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (m MINUS 12 TIMES FLOOR ((m MINUS 1) DIVIDED BY 12)) (DATE_YEAR d PLUS FLOOR ((m MINUS 1) DIVIDED BY 12))
    WHERE
        m MEANS DATE_MONTH d PLUS n PLUS 1

#ASSERT `the local authorities' determining date` EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 1999
#ASSERT `the earlier determining date the union's notice sets` (DATE_FROM_DMY 20 11 1999) EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2000
#ASSERT `the latest determining date the Finance Minister may publish` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2002) EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2003

§§ `פרק ב' §§3–9 — קופת גמל, חוק הפנסיה, החזר הוצאות, קרנות הפנסיה`

-- akn:chp_2__art_3 The heading of §3, the fund.
-- akn:chp_2__art_4 The heading of §4, the pension law.
-- akn:chp_2__art_4__para_d The heading "the three large cities".

-- §3 (א): the fund is a pension provident fund under the Income Tax
-- regulations of 1964 that is not an insurance fund; (ב) for an existing
-- employee who was an active member of managers' insurance on the eve of
-- the signing, and a new one who was on the eve of his coming — managers'
-- insurance (or, for the new one, either kind of pension fund). ¶2: "active"
-- is contributions made in the three months before the determining date,
-- or before he came.
@ref akn:chp_2__art_3__para_a akn:chp_2__art_3__para_b akn:chp_2__art_3__para_b/p2
DECLARE `1999 pension vehicle` IS ONE OF
    `a pension fund that is not an insurance fund`
    `managers' insurance`

GIVEN `active in managers' insurance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `1999 pension vehicle`
DECIDE `the fund of the 1999 agreement for` `active in managers' insurance` IS
    IF `active in managers' insurance`
    THEN `managers' insurance`
    ELSE `a pension fund that is not an insurance fund`

GIVEN `months of contributions in the three before` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an active member of managers' insurance by the 1999 agreement` `months of contributions in the three before` IF
    `months of contributions in the three before` AT LEAST 3

-- §4: the pension law each employer's budgetary pension is under — the
-- Pensions Law in the State, the Institute and the Service, and as adopted
-- by the fire-service associations and the three cities; §79 of the work
-- constitution at the local authorities and regional councils; the Jewish
-- Religious Services Law and the agreement of 1975 at the religious
-- councils; the Hebrew University's budgetary-pension agreement; the
-- Technion's pension constitution of 26.11.65. All outside the corpus.
@ref akn:chp_2__art_4__para_a akn:chp_2__art_4__para_b akn:chp_2__art_4__para_c akn:chp_2__art_4__para_d/p2 akn:chp_2__art_4__para_d/p3 akn:chp_2__art_4__para_d/p4 akn:chp_2__art_4__para_e akn:chp_2__art_4__para_f akn:chp_2__art_4__para_g
GIVEN e IS A `1999 transition employer`
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `the pension law of` e IS
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `a local authority of the Centre` THEN "סעיף 79 לחוקת העבודה לעובדי הרשויות המקומיות"
    WHEN `a regional council` THEN "סעיף 79 לחוקת העבודה לעובדי הרשויות המקומיות"
    WHEN `a religious council` THEN "חוק שירותי הדת היהודיים [נוסח משולב], התשל\"א-1971, וההסכם הקיבוצי משנת 1975"
    WHEN `the Hebrew University` THEN "הסכם הפנסיה התקציבית לעובדי האוניברסיטה העברית"
    WHEN `the Technion` THEN "חוקת הגימלאות מיום 26.11.65"
    OTHERWISE "חוק שירות המדינה (גמלאות) [נוסח משולב], התש\"ל-1970"

-- §5: "החזר הוצאות", every expense reimbursement — fixed or variable car
-- costs, the car's compulsory and comprehensive insurance and licence fee,
-- travel, subsistence, meals and the like; ¶2: at the Hebrew University
-- save the telephone reimbursement, pensionable at the determining date.
@ref akn:chp_2__art_5 akn:chp_2__art_5/p2
`the telephone reimbursement is an expense reimbursement at the Hebrew University` MEANS FALSE

-- §§6–9: an old accrual fund, approved before 1.1.1995; a new accrual fund,
-- approved after it and entitled to buy "ערד" bonds; a new general fund,
-- approved after it and not entitled to buy designated bonds; an accrual
-- fund, any of them by the agreement's rules.
@ref akn:chp_2__art_6 akn:chp_2__art_7 akn:chp_2__art_8 akn:chp_2__art_9
DECLARE `1999 accrual fund` IS ONE OF
    `an old accrual fund`
    `a new accrual fund`
    `a new general fund`

GIVEN `first approved on` IS A DATE, `may buy "ערד" bonds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `1999 accrual fund`
DECIDE `the kind of accrual fund by the 1999 agreement` `first approved on` `may buy "ערד" bonds` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `first approved on` `is on or after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1995) THEN `an old accrual fund`
        IF `may buy "ערד" bonds` THEN `a new accrual fund`
        OTHERWISE `a new general fund`

§§ `פרק ג' — תחולה`

-- akn:chp_3 The heading of chapter ג'.
-- akn:chp_3__art_1 The heading of §1.
-- akn:chp_3__art_3 The heading of §3.

-- §1(א): from the determining date the agreement covers every permanent,
-- existing and new employee of the employers, save (ב)'s, in the
-- workplaces where an employee could, until the determining date, join the
-- budgetary-pension track. (ב): physicians; the research staff of the
-- defence establishment and the Prime Minister's Office; universities'
-- academic staff; every scale of the security services (§63א of the
-- Pensions Law); the teaching scale represented by הסתדרות המורים or by
-- ארגון המורים. (ג): no dispute that it covers them at every local
-- authority, the three cities, the regional and the religious councils and
-- the fire-service associations. (ד): chapter ד' §7 applies from the
-- signing.
@ref akn:chp_3__art_1__para_a akn:chp_3__art_1__para_b akn:chp_3__art_1__para_c akn:chp_3__art_1__para_d
DECLARE `scale chapter ג' leaves out` IS ONE OF
    `the physicians' scale`
    `the defence and Prime Minister's Office research staff`
    `the universities' academic staff`
    `a scale of the security services`
    `the teaching scale represented by a teachers' union`
    `another scale`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the determining date` IS A DATE
      s IS A `1999 employee status`
      k IS A `scale chapter ג' leaves out`
      `the workplace had a budgetary track until the determining date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 1999 agreement covers` d `the determining date` s k `the workplace had a budgetary track until the determining date` IF
        d `is on or after` `the determining date`
    AND NOT s EQUALS `not an employee of the 1999 agreement`
    AND k EQUALS `another scale`
    AND `the workplace had a budgetary track until the determining date`

`the 1999 agreement's coverage is undisputed at the local authorities and the others of (ג)` MEANS TRUE

-- §2: it does not cover the workplaces whose employees were, until the
-- determining date and since, insured in an accrual pension by their own
-- agreement and could not join the budgetary track, tenure or no — what
-- §1(א)'s last condition already says.

@ref akn:chp_3__art_2
GIVEN `always in an accrual pension by its own agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 1999 agreement leaves out the workplace` `always in an accrual pension by its own agreement` IF
    `always in an accrual pension by its own agreement`

-- §3(א): at other employers that are budgeted or supported bodies under the
-- Budget Foundations Law (imported: its §§21 and 32), in a workplace whose
-- employees could join the budgetary track on the signing, if a move to an
-- accrual pension is agreed there, this agreement is carried out, within
-- its cost; (ב) at the others, only with the wages commissioner's
-- approval, by his letter of 3.3.99 (outside the corpus); the Treasury's
-- signature approves nothing for an employer that did not sign.
@ref akn:chp_3__art_3__para_a akn:chp_3__art_3__para_b
GIVEN b IS AN `employing body`
      `its employees could join the budgetary track on the signing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a move to an accrual pension is agreed there` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the wages commissioner approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 1999 agreement is carried out at another employer` b `its employees could join the budgetary track on the signing` `a move to an accrual pension is agreed there` `the wages commissioner approved` IF
        (`is a budgeted body` b OR `is a supported body` b)
    AND (   (`its employees could join the budgetary track on the signing` AND `a move to an accrual pension is agreed there`)
         OR `the wages commissioner approved`)

§§ `פרק ד' — עובד קבוע`

-- akn:chp_4 The heading of chapter ד'.
-- akn:chp_4__art_3 The heading of §3.
-- akn:chp_4__art_6 The heading of §6.

-- §1: permanent employees stay on the budgetary-pension track.
@ref akn:chp_4__art_1
GIVEN s IS A `1999 employee status`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `stays on the budgetary-pension track` s IF
    s EQUALS `a permanent employee`

-- A salary component, as chapters ד' and ו' tell them apart.
DECLARE `1999 salary component` IS ONE OF
    `a component of the budgetary determining salary`
    `havraa pay`
    `the clothing allowance`
    `the jubilee grant`
    `an expense reimbursement`
    `a tax gross-up`
    `a benefit imputed for tax`
    `another salary component`

`the 1999 components` MEANS
    LIST `a component of the budgetary determining salary`, `havraa pay`, `the clothing allowance`, `the jubilee grant`, `an expense reimbursement`, `a tax gross-up`, `a benefit imputed for tax`, `another salary component`

-- §2: "the determining salary for a budgetary pension" here is the
-- determining salary on that track, and the havraa pay, clothing allowance
-- and jubilee grant paid to its pensioners.
@ref akn:chp_4__art_2
GIVEN c IS A `1999 salary component`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `in the budgetary determining salary of chapter ד'` c IF
       c EQUALS `a component of the budgetary determining salary`
    OR c EQUALS `havraa pay`
    OR c EQUALS `the clothing allowance`
    OR c EQUALS `the jubilee grant`

-- §3(א): from the determining date, for permanent employees, contributions
-- go to a new accrual fund up to the monthly ceiling of insured salary the
-- law allows, and above it to a new general fund; the base is every
-- component outside §2's determining salary that is not an expense
-- reimbursement, a tax gross-up or a benefit imputed for tax. (ב): a
-- permanent employee who asks has them all go to a new general fund. (ג):
-- the parties may discuss where contributions on components that do not
-- exist at the determining date go.
@ref akn:chp_4__art_3__para_a akn:chp_4__art_3__para_b akn:chp_4__art_3__para_c
GIVEN c IS A `1999 salary component`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `in a permanent employee's accrual base` c IF
        NOT `in the budgetary determining salary of chapter ד'` c
    AND NOT c EQUALS `an expense reimbursement`
    AND NOT c EQUALS `a tax gross-up`
    AND NOT c EQUALS `a benefit imputed for tax`

@desc How much of the insured salary goes to which fund.
DECLARE `1999 split between funds` HAS
    `to the new accrual fund` IS A NUMBER
    `to the new general fund` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the insured salary` IS A NUMBER
      `the monthly ceiling the law allows` IS A NUMBER
      `asked for the general fund alone` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `1999 split between funds`
DECIDE `the 1999 split of a permanent employee's insured salary` `the insured salary` `the monthly ceiling the law allows` `asked for the general fund alone` IS
    IF `asked for the general fund alone`
    THEN `1999 split between funds` WITH
             `to the new accrual fund` IS 0
             `to the new general fund` IS `the insured salary`
    ELSE `1999 split between funds` WITH
             `to the new accrual fund` IS min `the insured salary` `the monthly ceiling the law allows`
             `to the new general fund` IS `not below zero` (`the insured salary` MINUS `the monthly ceiling the law allows`)

`the parties may discuss the channel for components new after the determining date` MEANS TRUE

-- §4: the agreement changes nothing in the budgetary pension's base and
-- its update — "the determining salary" and "a fixed supplement" of §8 of
-- the Pensions Law among them. §5: a component in it at the determining
-- date stays in it and does not move to the accrual contributions.
@ref akn:chp_4__art_4 akn:chp_4__art_5
`the 1999 agreement changes the budgetary pension's base` MEANS FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `in a permanent employee's accrual base` `a component of the budgetary determining salary`

-- §6(א): for permanent employees §3 takes the place of the provident-fund
-- agreement of 10.8.95 ("הסכם הגמל", not yet encoded) for the components it
-- brings into the accrual fund, from the start of those contributions. (ב):
-- the contributions to a provident fund (employees') under it go on, for a
-- permanent employee, on every expense reimbursement save the gross-up and
-- the imputed benefit — none on the clothing, havraa and jubilee paid to
-- budgetary pensioners — its other rules unchanged. (ג): never twice on one
-- component for one period, to a provident fund and an accrual fund.
@ref akn:chp_4__art_6__para_a akn:chp_4__art_6__para_b akn:chp_4__art_6__para_b/p2 akn:chp_4__art_6__para_c
GIVEN c IS A `1999 salary component`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provident-fund agreement goes on for a permanent employee on` c IF
    c EQUALS `an expense reimbursement`

GIVEN c IS A `1999 salary component`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `contributed twice for a permanent employee on` c IF
    `the provident-fund agreement goes on for a permanent employee on` c AND `in a permanent employee's accrual base` c

#ASSERT all (GIVEN c YIELD NOT `contributed twice for a permanent employee on` c) `the 1999 components`

-- §7 (from the signing, chapter ג' §1(ד)): a permanent employee who moves,
-- even after the determining date, to an employer that had a budgetary
-- track until then stays on it there, by the continuity agreements in
-- force at the signing (outside the corpus), which it neither takes from
-- nor adds to.
@ref akn:chp_4__art_7 akn:chp_4__art_7/p2
GIVEN `moves to an employer that had a budgetary track` IS A BOOLEAN, `the continuity agreements keep him on it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a moving permanent employee stays on the budgetary track` `moves to an employer that had a budgetary track` `the continuity agreements keep him on it` IF
    `moves to an employer that had a budgetary track` AND `the continuity agreements keep him on it`

`chapter ד' §7 applies from` MEANS `the pension-transition agreement was signed on`

-- §8: a permanent employee may ask that from the determining date 7% of
-- every component of §3's base go to a new account in a provident fund for
-- the self-employed ("ההסדר החליפי"); it takes, for him, the place of §§3
-- and 6, and comes on top of the 5% and 5% to the employees' provident fund
-- on every component outside the budgetary determining salary save the
-- gross-up and the imputed benefit, under the agreement of 10.8.95 — in
-- place of its §13.
@ref akn:chp_4__art_8 akn:chp_4__art_8/p2 akn:chp_4__art_8/p3
`the alternative arrangement's rate for the self-employed fund` MEANS 7%
`the employer's provident-fund rate beside the alternative arrangement` MEANS 5%
`the employee's provident-fund rate beside the alternative arrangement` MEANS 5%

GIVEN `the base of §3` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the alternative arrangement's monthly contribution` `the base of §3` IS
    `the alternative arrangement's rate for the self-employed fund` TIMES `the base of §3`

-- §9 ¶1: if after the determining date the budgetary determining salary
-- takes in a component it did not on the eve, on which contributions were
-- made under this agreement or the agreement of 10.8.95, they stop, and the
-- employer has his share back, by the capital market's rules. ¶2: if a
-- permanent employee is in fact paid a budgetary pension on a component
-- that carried contributions for the same period, the parties discuss how
-- the employer's share comes back; ¶3: chapter ט"ז applies.
@ref akn:chp_4__art_9 akn:chp_4__art_9/p2 akn:chp_4__art_9/p3
GIVEN `the determining salary took it in` IS A BOOLEAN, `contributions were made on it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contributions on the component stop and the employer has his share back` `the determining salary took it in` `contributions were made on it` IF
    `the determining salary took it in` AND `contributions were made on it`

GIVEN `paid a budgetary pension on a component that carried contributions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `1999 transition action`
DECIDE `returning the employer's share on a pensioned component` `paid a budgetary pension on a component that carried contributions` IS
    IF `paid a budgetary pension on a component that carried contributions`
    THEN PARTY `the employer`
         MUST  `discuss returning the employer's share on a component the budgetary pension pays`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- §10: the employers agree to sign a completeness agreement with the
-- pension funds, in a text agreed within 30 days of the signing, on the
-- principles of annexes ג1 and ג2 (below); it is then annexed.
@ref akn:chp_4__art_10
`signing the completeness agreement` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `sign the completeness agreement with the pension funds`
    WITHIN 30

§§ `פרק ה' — עובד קיים ועובד חדש`

-- akn:chp_5 The heading of chapter ה'.
-- akn:chp_5__art_3 The heading of §3.

-- §1: existing employees stay insured in an accrual fund, from the
-- determining date on chapter ו' §1(א)'s base; §2: new employees are
-- insured in a comprehensive pension in an accrual fund.
@ref akn:chp_5__art_1 akn:chp_5__art_2
GIVEN s IS A `1999 employee status`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `insured in an accrual fund by chapter ה'` s IF
    s EQUALS `an existing employee` OR s EQUALS `a new employee`

-- §3(א): notwithstanding, an existing employee actively insured in
-- managers' insurance on the eve of the signing, and a new one who was on
-- the eve of his coming and tells the employer in writing within 14 days,
-- stay in it, and chapter י' does not apply to them. (ב): such an employee
-- may tell the employer in writing at any time that he wishes to be in an
-- accrual fund, from the 1st of the month after his notice, by chapter
-- י'. ¶2: until then, his insurance follows each employer's custom on the
-- eve, as it may be — its rates among it — the existing employee not
-- harmed; the agreement applies to him as fitted: (1) further components;
-- (2) money back under chapter ט'; (3) where the employer contributes under
-- the Minister of Labour's order (י"פ 4659), the contributions take the
-- place of severance by its terms. "An accrual fund" reads "managers'
-- insurance" for him, save in these matters, and the employer may deduct
-- his share.
@ref akn:chp_5__art_3__para_a akn:chp_5__art_3__para_b akn:chp_5__art_3__para_b/p2 akn:chp_5__art_3__para_b__subpara_1 akn:chp_5__art_3__para_b__subpara_2 akn:chp_5__art_3__para_b__subpara_3 akn:chp_5__art_3__para_b__subpara_3/p2 akn:chp_5__art_3__para_b__subpara_3/p3
GIVEN s IS A `1999 employee status`
      `active in managers' insurance on the eve` IS A BOOLEAN
      `days a new employee took to tell the employer` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `stays in managers' insurance under chapter ה' §3` s `active in managers' insurance on the eve` `days a new employee took to tell the employer` IF
        `active in managers' insurance on the eve`
    AND (   s EQUALS `an existing employee`
         OR (s EQUALS `a new employee` AND `days a new employee took to tell the employer` AT MOST 14))

GIVEN `the day of his notice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `moves from managers' insurance to an accrual fund from` `the day of his notice` IS
    `the first of the month after` 0 `months after the month of` `the day of his notice`

#ASSERT `moves from managers' insurance to an accrual fund from` (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 5 2000) EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2000

§§ `פרק ו' — הבסיס להפרשה לעובדים קיימים וחדשים`

-- akn:chp_6 The heading of chapter ו'.
-- akn:chp_6__art_1 The heading of §1.
-- akn:chp_6__art_3 The heading of §3.

-- §1(א): from the determining date the base for existing and new
-- employees is both (1) the budgetary determining salary of a permanent
-- employee, save the clothing allowance and with the jubilee grant and
-- havraa pay, and (2) every other component that is not an expense
-- reimbursement, a tax gross-up or an imputed benefit, and not the clothing
-- allowance. (ב): the parties may discuss the channel for components new
-- after the determining date.
@ref akn:chp_6__art_1__para_a akn:chp_6__art_1__para_a__subpara_1 akn:chp_6__art_1__para_a__subpara_2 akn:chp_6__art_1__para_b
GIVEN c IS A `1999 salary component`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `in an existing or new employee's accrual base` c IF
        NOT c EQUALS `the clothing allowance`
    AND NOT c EQUALS `an expense reimbursement`
    AND NOT c EQUALS `a tax gross-up`
    AND NOT c EQUALS `a benefit imputed for tax`

-- §2: an existing or new employee in an old accrual fund is insured in it
-- on the components of §1(א)(2) too.
@ref akn:chp_6__art_2
GIVEN `his fund` IS A `1999 accrual fund`
GIVETH A `1999 accrual fund`
DECIDE `the fund the further components go to` `his fund` IS `his fund`

-- §3(א)–(ג): §1(א)(2) takes the place of the agreement of 10.8.95 for its
-- components; the contributions to the employees' provident fund go on, or
-- start, on every expense reimbursement and on the clothing allowance, save
-- the gross-up and the imputed benefit; never twice. (ד): the cost frame of
-- the agreement of 10.8.95, its annex ו' §4 among it, does not apply to the
-- employees chapter ד' §3 and chapter ו' §1(א) reach.
@ref akn:chp_6__art_3__para_a akn:chp_6__art_3__para_b akn:chp_6__art_3__para_b/p2 akn:chp_6__art_3__para_c akn:chp_6__art_3__para_d
GIVEN c IS A `1999 salary component`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provident-fund agreement goes on for an existing or new employee on` c IF
    c EQUALS `an expense reimbursement` OR c EQUALS `the clothing allowance`

#ASSERT all (GIVEN c YIELD NOT (`the provident-fund agreement goes on for an existing or new employee on` c AND `in an existing or new employee's accrual base` c)) `the 1999 components`

`the cost frame of the agreement of 10.8.95 reaches those this agreement insures` MEANS FALSE

-- §4: the agreement and its contributions change nothing each employer did
-- until the determining date about the budgetary determining salary, the
-- components counted for severance, those the training fund is paid on,
-- and the hour value.
@ref akn:chp_6__art_4 akn:chp_6__art_4__para_a akn:chp_6__art_4__para_b akn:chp_6__art_4__para_c akn:chp_6__art_4__para_d
DECLARE `what chapter ו' §4 leaves as it was` IS ONE OF
    `the budgetary determining salary`
    `the components counted for severance`
    `the components of the training fund`
    `the hour value`

GIVEN w IS A `what chapter ו' §4 leaves as it was`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 1999 contributions change` w IF FALSE

#ASSERT `in an existing or new employee's accrual base` `havraa pay`
#ASSERT NOT `in an existing or new employee's accrual base` `the clothing allowance`
#ASSERT NOT `in a permanent employee's accrual base` `havraa pay`

§§ `פרק ז' — ההפרשות לקרן פנסיה צוברת`

-- akn:chp_7 The heading of chapter ז'.
-- akn:chp_7__art_1 The heading of §1.

-- §1(א): from the determining date the employer contributes 12% of the
-- insured salary (chapter ד' §3 for a permanent employee, chapter ו' §1(א)
-- for existing and new ones) every month, for benefits and in place of
-- severance by the Income Tax regulations' rates; (ב): and deducts 5.5%.
@ref akn:chp_7__art_1__para_a akn:chp_7__art_1__para_b
`the employer's accrual contribution under the 1999 agreement` MEANS 12%
`the employee's accrual deduction under the 1999 agreement` MEANS 5.5%

-- §2: an existing employee of a local-government employer (the local
-- authorities, the three cities, the regional and religious councils, the
-- fire-service associations) has, subject to the Treasury capital-market
-- approval of annex ד': (א) for up to a year of his work before the
-- determining date that carried basic-pension contributions to an old fund
-- (6% and 5.5%), a retroactive rise to 17.5% (12% and 5.5%) at the
-- employer's cost, the period counting for a comprehensive pension; (ב) for
-- his work from the start of the determining date's tax year that carried
-- some contribution to a new fund, completion to 17.5%; (ג) for that work
-- with none, a retroactive 17.5% — on the components it was customary to
-- insure; (ד) where (ב)–(ג)'s period is under 12 months, for the rest to 12:
-- (1) once continuity agreements with the new funds are signed, the
-- employer funds the payments (2) the fund computes, at an insured event,
-- the difference between his pension and the one full comprehensive
-- contributions for the rest would have given, (3) the employer transfers
-- it and the fund pays him; (4) failing that, the parties negotiate another
-- arrangement, costing no more than the contributions would have.
@ref akn:chp_7__art_2 akn:chp_7__art_2__para_a akn:chp_7__art_2__para_b akn:chp_7__art_2__para_c akn:chp_7__art_2__para_d akn:chp_7__art_2__para_d__subpara_1 akn:chp_7__art_2__para_d__subpara_2 akn:chp_7__art_2__para_d__subpara_3 akn:chp_7__art_2__para_d__subpara_4 akn:chp_7__art_2/p2
`the full comprehensive rate of the 1999 agreement` MEANS 17.5%
`the basic-pension employer's rate in an old fund` MEANS 6%

#ASSERT `the full comprehensive rate of the 1999 agreement` EQUALS `the employer's accrual contribution under the 1999 agreement` PLUS `the employee's accrual deduction under the 1999 agreement`

GIVEN `months of the completed period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the months the local-government arrangement covers beyond the completion` `months of the completed period` IS
    `not below zero` (12 MINUS `months of the completed period`)

GIVEN `the pension with full contributions` IS A NUMBER, `the pension he is entitled to` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the difference the employer transfers to the fund` `the pension with full contributions` `the pension he is entitled to` IS
    `not below zero` (`the pension with full contributions` MINUS `the pension he is entitled to`)

GIVEN `the continuity agreements allow it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `1999 transition action`
DECIDE `the rest of the year when the funds cannot pay` `the continuity agreements allow it` IS
    IF `the continuity agreements allow it`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the employer`
         MUST  `negotiate another arrangement for the rest of the year`

-- §3: new employees of local government are insured from their start on
-- chapter ו' §1's components at §1's rates.
@ref akn:chp_7__art_3
`a new local-government employee is insured from his start` MEANS TRUE

§§ `פרק ח' — השלמה לפיצויי פיטורין`

-- akn:chp_8 The heading of chapter ח'.

-- (1): for existing and new employees the contributions in place of
-- severance take the place of the whole 72% of severance under §14 of the
-- Severance Pay Law, on the components counted for severance that carried
-- contributions; (2) the employer pays the rest, 28% of those components of
-- the last salary times his seniority, at an event entitling to severance
-- or at the end of work with a pension from the fund — and to one not
-- entitled to a pension for want of the minimum; (3) a component that
-- carried no contribution keeps the whole statutory severance; (4) so does
-- a period with no contribution, or one at basic-pension rates; (5) none of
-- this for a permanent employee on the budgetary track, whose employer's
-- rules apply.
@ref akn:chp_8__para_1 akn:chp_8__para_2 akn:chp_8__para_3 akn:chp_8__para_4 akn:chp_8__para_5
`the share of severance the contributions take the place of` MEANS 72%
`the share of severance the employer pays at the end` MEANS 28%

#ASSERT `the share of severance the contributions take the place of` PLUS `the share of severance the employer pays at the end` EQUALS 1

GIVEN s IS A `1999 employee status`
      `the last salary's components that carried contributions` IS A NUMBER
      `years of seniority` IS A NUMBER
      `an entitling event or a pension from the fund` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the severance completion of chapter ח'` s `the last salary's components that carried contributions` `years of seniority` `an entitling event or a pension from the fund` IS
    IF     (s EQUALS `an existing employee` OR s EQUALS `a new employee`)
       AND `an entitling event or a pension from the fund`
    THEN `the share of severance the employer pays at the end` TIMES `the last salary's components that carried contributions` TIMES `years of seniority`
    ELSE 0

#ASSERT `the severance completion of chapter ח'` `a new employee` 10000 10 TRUE EQUALS 28000
#ASSERT `the severance completion of chapter ח'` `a permanent employee` 10000 10 TRUE EQUALS 0

§§ `פרק ט' — משיכת כספים מקרן הפנסיה ע"י המעסיק`

-- akn:chp_9 The heading of chapter ט'.

-- The fund returns, and the employer may ask for, half (6%) of the
-- contributions the employer paid, on the Income Tax regulations' terms,
-- where the employee resigned or was dismissed with no right to severance,
-- left the fund and drew his money; with only partial severance, the share
-- of the 6% the partial severance leaves.
@ref akn:chp_9/p1
`the share of the employer's contributions that may come back` MEANS 6%

#ASSERT `the share of the employer's contributions that may come back` EQUALS `the employer's accrual contribution under the 1999 agreement` DIVIDED BY 2

GIVEN `the share of severance he was entitled to` IS A NUMBER @desc 0 with no right to severance, 1 with full
      `left the fund and drew his money` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the rate that comes back to the employer` `the share of severance he was entitled to` `left the fund and drew his money` IS
    IF `left the fund and drew his money` AND `the share of severance he was entitled to` LESS THAN 1
    THEN `the share of the employer's contributions that may come back` TIMES (1 MINUS `the share of severance he was entitled to`)
    ELSE 0

§§ `פרק י' — בחירת קרן פנסיה צוברת`

-- akn:chp_10 The heading of chapter י'.

-- §1: the union tells the employer the fund or funds it chose. §2: one not
-- insured in an accrual fund until the determining date, or on starting
-- after it, is insured in the union's fund unless he tells the employer in
-- writing of another; §3: one insured in a fund other than the union's
-- stays in it unless he tells of the union's or another; §4: his right by
-- law to move between funds is kept; §5: from the determining date.
@ref akn:chp_10__art_1 akn:chp_10__art_2 akn:chp_10__art_3 akn:chp_10__art_4 akn:chp_10__art_5
`telling the employer of the chosen funds` MEANS
    PARTY `the New General Histadrut`
    MUST  `notify the employer of the chosen pension funds`

GIVEN `the union's fund` IS A STRING
      `the fund he is insured in` IS A MAYBE STRING
      `the fund he told the employer of` IS A MAYBE STRING
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `the fund an employee is insured in by chapter י'` `the union's fund` `the fund he is insured in` `the fund he told the employer of` IS
    CONSIDER `the fund he told the employer of`
    WHEN JUST told THEN told
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER `the fund he is insured in`
        WHEN JUST insured THEN insured
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `the union's fund`

#ASSERT `the fund an employee is insured in by chapter י'` "א" NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS "א"
#ASSERT `the fund an employee is insured in by chapter י'` "א" (JUST "ב") NOTHING EQUALS "ב"
#ASSERT `the fund an employee is insured in by chapter י'` "א" (JUST "ב") (JUST "ג") EQUALS "ג"

§§ `פרק יא' — מסגרת עלות`

-- akn:chp_11 The heading of chapter י"א.

-- §1: "cost" here is the rise of the employer's contributions from 5% to
-- 12% on the components moved from the employees' provident fund to an
-- accrual fund, or by the alternative arrangement; ¶2: the agreement's cost
-- is 2.1% of the budgetary-pension salary base, on 1997's data, for the
-- components that exist. §2: no reckoning between the parties over it,
-- even if those components change after the determining date.
@ref akn:chp_11__art_1 akn:chp_11__art_1/p2 akn:chp_11__art_2
`the rise of the employer's contribution chapter י"א counts` MEANS
    `the employer's accrual contribution under the 1999 agreement` MINUS `the employer's provident-fund rate beside the alternative arrangement`

`the cost of the 1999 agreement` MEANS 2.1%

`the parties reckon over the 1999 agreement's cost` MEANS FALSE

#ASSERT `the rise of the employer's contribution chapter י"א counts` EQUALS 7%
#ASSERT `the rise of the employer's contribution chapter י"א counts` EQUALS `the alternative arrangement's rate for the self-employed fund`

§§ `פרקים יב'–יט'`

-- akn:chp_12 The heading of chapter י"ב.
-- akn:chp_13 The heading of chapter י"ג.
-- akn:chp_14 The heading of chapter י"ד.
-- akn:chp_16 The heading of chapter ט"ז.
-- akn:chp_17 The heading of chapter י"ז.
-- akn:chp_18 The heading of chapter י"ח.
-- akn:chp_19 The heading of chapter י"ט.

-- י"ב ¶1: the parties support the steps, legislation among them, that
-- carry out the agreement; the bill of annex ה' expresses its principles,
-- and the government (the Treasury, which drafted it) acts to advance it.
-- ¶2: the Histadrut's signature
-- approves the changes each employer needs to carry it out.
@ref akn:chp_12/p1 akn:chp_12/p2
`supporting the transition` MEANS
    PARTY `the New General Histadrut`
    MUST  `support the steps the transition agreement needs`

`advancing the bill` MEANS
    PARTY `the Treasury`
    MUST  `act to advance the bill amending the Pensions Law`

-- י"ג §1: if an agreement on the move from a budgetary to an accrual
-- pension with another union, for a group this one does not cover, sets
-- different or better terms, every benefit and better term in it applies
-- to these employees too, subject to §2 and from when it applies there —
-- a right of the Histadrut, at its discretion. §2: only (א) the difference
-- of the whole cost in percent of the pension salary — not counting a cost
-- the employer bears by an agreement with another union, made by the
-- signing, that is not about the move (this agreement's: 2.1%); and (ב)
-- terms with no cost.
@ref akn:chp_13__art_1 akn:chp_13__art_1/p2 akn:chp_13__art_2 akn:chp_13__art_2__para_a akn:chp_13__art_2__para_a/p2 akn:chp_13__art_2__para_a/p3 akn:chp_13__art_2__para_b
`the whole cost of the 1999 agreement for chapter י"ג` MEANS 2.1%

#ASSERT `the whole cost of the 1999 agreement for chapter י"ג` EQUALS `the cost of the 1999 agreement`

GIVEN `the other agreement's cost` IS A NUMBER, `the Histadrut chose to claim it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the cost difference chapter י"ג equalises` `the other agreement's cost` `the Histadrut chose to claim it` IS
    IF `the Histadrut chose to claim it`
    THEN `not below zero` (`the other agreement's cost` MINUS `the whole cost of the 1999 agreement for chapter י"ג`)
    ELSE 0

#ASSERT `the cost difference chapter י"ג equalises` (2.5%) TRUE EQUALS 0.4%

-- י"ד: earlier terms are neither added to nor taken from, unless it changes
-- or cancels them. ט"ו: signed following the summary of 8.12.1997,
-- government decision 4845 of 7.2.99 and the wages commissioner's notice of
-- 3.3.99 on posts in the civil service, the Service and the Institute
-- (outside the corpus), taking nothing from them.
@ref akn:chp_14/p1 akn:chp_15
`earlier terms stand unless the 1999 agreement changes them` MEANS TRUE

-- ט"ז: a follow-up committee of the chair of the Histadrut's trade-union
-- department and the wages commissioner follows and helps carry it out and
-- decides disputes, after hearing those concerned; ¶2: where it agrees, its
-- decision is final.
@ref akn:chp_16/p1 akn:chp_16/p2
`deciding disputes over the transition agreement` MEANS
    PARTY `the follow-up committee`
    MUST  `decide disputes over the transition agreement`

`the follow-up committee's agreed decision on the transition agreement is final` MEANS TRUE

-- י"ז: it starts on the determining date, save chapter ד' §7, from the
-- signing. י"ח: the parties' claims on the move are exhausted, subject to
-- chapter י"ג. י"ט: it is submitted for registration.
@ref akn:chp_17/p1 akn:chp_18/p1 akn:chp_19/p1
GIVEN d IS A DATE, `the determining date` IS A DATE, `chapter ד' §7` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 1999 provision is in force on` d `the determining date` `chapter ד' §7` IF
    IF `chapter ד' §7`
    THEN d `is on or after` `chapter ד' §7 applies from`
    ELSE d `is on or after` `the determining date`

`registering the transition agreement` MEANS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `submit the transition agreement for registration`

