-- The principles of buying rights back in time, for members of the funds,
-- the municipalities and the Centre among them: (א) in a new fund, (1) for
-- a year back at most, (2) at full actuarial balance and market interest,
-- (3) with linkage and interest from when it was due to the day paid; (ב)
-- in an old fund likewise, but (1) for up to 24 months, subject to the 1964
-- regulations, the commissioner's directions and the fund's rules, and (2)
-- a move from a basic to a comprehensive pension back in time, for up to 24
-- months, at full actuarial balance and market interest, for every employee.
@ref akn:att_5__hc_1/p12 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_a akn:att_5__hc_1__para_a__subpara_1 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_a__subpara_2 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_a__subpara_3 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_b akn:att_5__hc_1__para_b__subpara_1 akn:att_5__hc_1__para_b__subpara_2
GIVEN k IS A `1999 accrual fund`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the months back rights may be bought in` k IS
    IF k EQUALS `an old accrual fund` THEN 24 ELSE 12

#ASSERT `the months back rights may be bought in` `a new accrual fund` EQUALS 12
-- Chapter ז' §2(א)'s year back is within annex ד''s.
#ASSERT 12 AT MOST `the months back rights may be bought in` `an old accrual fund`

§§ `נספח ה' — הצעת חוק שירות המדינה (גימלאות) (מעבר לפנסיה צוברת)`

-- akn:att_6__hc_1/p1 The State of Israel; no rule.
-- akn:att_6__hc_1/p2 The Treasury; no rule.
-- akn:att_6__hc_1/p3 The wages unit; no rule.
-- akn:att_6__hc_1/p4 The file number; no rule.
