-- The first letter: once the transition is carried out in full for every
-- employee the Histadrut represents at every signing employer save the two
-- universities (the hospitals, ממ"ג and רפא"ל among them), the commissioner
-- will approve a request of a budgeted or supported body — whose new
-- employees could not, at the signing, join the budgetary track, and that
-- applies the agreement of 10.8.95 with his approval — to widen the base
-- insured in an accrual pension: (1) at a cost of up to 0.5% of the pension
-- salary beyond the wage agreements', (2) only for the time after the
-- approval; not conditioned on the cost frame of annex ו' §4 of 10.8.95;
-- he acts on a full request within two months.
@ref akn:att_7__hc_1/p11 akn:att_7__hc_1__para_1 akn:att_7__hc_1__para_2 akn:att_7__hc_1/p12 akn:att_7__hc_1/p13
`the most widening the base at a budgeted body may cost` MEANS 0.5%

GIVEN `the transition is carried out in full` IS A BOOLEAN, `the cost` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the commissioner approves widening the base at a budgeted body` `the transition is carried out in full` `the cost` IF
    `the transition is carried out in full` AND `the cost` AT MOST `the most widening the base at a budgeted body may cost`

`approving a request to widen the base` MEANS
    PARTY `the wages commissioner`
    MUST  `approve a request to widen the insured base`
    WITHIN 61

-- akn:att_8__hc_1/p1 The corpus's label for the wages commissioner's letter on widening the insured base where employees were in an accrual pension; no rule.
