-- The general agreement on §79 of the work constitution (pensions): (1) §79
-- is changed by, and subject to, the transition agreement — which it names
-- "מיום 3.4.99" (F-pension-1999-a); (2) from the Centre's determining date.
@ref akn:att_10__hc_1__para_1 akn:att_10__hc_1__para_2
`the day the §79 agreement names the transition agreement by` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 3 4 1999

`§79 changes at the local authorities from` MEANS `the local authorities' determining date`

§§ `illustrations`

-- Chapter ב' §1: a State employee with a §17 letter, permanent; one under
-- a permit in an accrual pension, permanent too (F-pension-1999-b); one in
-- an accrual pension with neither, existing; one taken on after, new.
GIVEN employed IS A BOOLEAN, appointed IS A BOOLEAN, permit IS A BOOLEAN, accrual IS A BOOLEAN, manual IS A BOOLEAN, months IS A NUMBER, transient IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `1999 employee facts`
DECIDE `an example employee` employed appointed permit accrual manual months transient IS
    `1999 employee facts` WITH
        `left out of "עובד" at his employer`                    IS FALSE
        `employed at the determining date`                     IS employed
        `insured in an accrual pension at the determining date` IS accrual
        `appointed or tenured by the determining date`         IS appointed
        `employed under a written permit of §§37, 38 or 39א`   IS permit
        `on probation in a standard post`                      IS FALSE
        `appointed or tenured after the determining date`      IS FALSE
        `a manual worker`                                      IS manual
        `months employed by the employer`                      IS months
        `in a standard post`                                   IS TRUE
        `months in that post`                                  IS months
        `in a transient post`                                  IS transient
        `completed a year with the authority`                  IS TRUE
        `chose an accrual pension on tenure`                   IS FALSE
        `completed his probation`                              IS TRUE
        `on a fixed-term personal contract`                    IS FALSE

`a State employee's facts` MEANS `an example employee` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 60 FALSE
`a permit holder in an accrual pension` MEANS `an example employee` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE 60 FALSE
`an employee in an accrual pension with no letter or permit` MEANS `an example employee` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE 60 FALSE
`an employee taken on after the determining date` MEANS `an example employee` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE

#ASSERT `the 1999 status of` `the State's service` `a State employee's facts` FALSE EQUALS `a permanent employee`
#ASSERT `the 1999 status of` `the State's service` `a permit holder in an accrual pension` FALSE EQUALS `a permanent employee`
#ASSERT `the 1999 status of` `the State's service` `an employee in an accrual pension with no letter or permit` FALSE EQUALS `an existing employee`
#ASSERT `the 1999 status of` `the State's service` `an employee taken on after the determining date` FALSE EQUALS `a new employee`
#ASSERT `the 1999 status of` `a local authority of the Centre` `an employee in an accrual pension with no letter or permit` FALSE EQUALS `an existing employee`
#ASSERT `the 1999 status of` `a local authority of the Centre` `a State employee's facts` FALSE EQUALS `a permanent employee`

-- F-pension-1999-b's evidence: the permit holder in an accrual pension
-- meets both definitions as printed.
`a permit holder in an accrual pension is both permanent and existing in the State` MEANS
        `permanent in the State's service by the 1999 definition` `a permit holder in an accrual pension`
    AND `a permit holder in an accrual pension`'s `insured in an accrual pension at the determining date`
    AND `the 1999 status of` `the State's service` `a permit holder in an accrual pension` FALSE EQUALS `a permanent employee`
#ASSERT `a permit holder in an accrual pension is both permanent and existing in the State`

-- F-pension-1999-c's evidence: a Tel Aviv manual worker of 30 months in a
-- transient post meets both definitions as printed; read as existing.
`a Tel Aviv transient post of 30 months` MEANS `an example employee` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 30 TRUE

`a Tel Aviv transient post past the months is both permanent and existing` MEANS
        `permanent in Tel Aviv by the 1999 definition, as printed` `a Tel Aviv transient post of 30 months`
    AND `existing in Tel Aviv by the 1999 definition, as printed` `a Tel Aviv transient post of 30 months`
    AND `the 1999 status of` `the Tel Aviv municipality` `a Tel Aviv transient post of 30 months` FALSE EQUALS `an existing employee`
#ASSERT `a Tel Aviv transient post past the months is both permanent and existing`

-- F-pension-1999-a's evidence: the annexed agreement names the transition
-- agreement by a day a month after the one the corpus dates it by.
`the §79 agreement names a day the transition agreement was not signed on` MEANS
    NOT `the day the §79 agreement names the transition agreement by` EQUALS `the pension-transition agreement was signed on`
#ASSERT `the §79 agreement names a day the transition agreement was not signed on`

-- Chapter ד' §3: a permanent employee's 20,000 insured over a ceiling of
-- 15,000: 15,000 to the new accrual fund, 5,000 to the general one.
`15,000 and 5,000` MEANS
    `1999 split between funds` WITH
        `to the new accrual fund` IS 15000
        `to the new general fund` IS 5000
`none and 20,000` MEANS
    `1999 split between funds` WITH
        `to the new accrual fund` IS 0
        `to the new general fund` IS 20000
#ASSERT `the 1999 split of a permanent employee's insured salary` 20000 15000 FALSE EQUALS `15,000 and 5,000`
#ASSERT `the 1999 split of a permanent employee's insured salary` 20000 15000 TRUE EQUALS `none and 20,000`

-- Chapter ג': a teaching employee the teachers' unions represent is not
-- covered.
#ASSERT NOT `the 1999 agreement covers` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 8 1999) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 1999) `a new employee` `the teaching scale represented by a teachers' union` TRUE
#ASSERT `the 1999 agreement covers` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 8 1999) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 1999) `a new employee` `another scale` TRUE
#ASSERT `the 1999 agreement is carried out at another employer` `a municipal company` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the 1999 agreement is carried out at another employer` `another employer` TRUE TRUE FALSE

-- Chapter ט': dismissed with half the severance, 3% comes back.
#ASSERT `the rate that comes back to the employer` 0.5 TRUE EQUALS 3%
#ASSERT `the rate that comes back to the employer` 1 TRUE EQUALS 0
